    {
      "block_id": "2605.22715_p6_b13",
      "text": "We update codebooks with exponential moving averages and refresh dead codes to maintain codebook\nusage. Finally, the IMU token sequence is formed by interleaving product-code indices over time,\ns = [\u03ba1,1, . . . , \u03ba1,P , \u03ba2,1, . . . , \u03baT \u2032,P ]. These discrete tokens preserve the temporal order of the setup-\nstable motion latent and serve as the IMU input tokens for motion-language alignment in Section 3.3.\nSince both G\u03b8 and the tokenizer operate temporally, variable-length IMU windows are handled by\nproducing variable-length token sequences.\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.53,
        202.01,
        505.74,
        266.44
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
